# Vauxhall Cavalier Mk3 four-door saloon, 1988-1995.
#
# The last Cavalier: the Vectra A twin, launched to dealers from 24 August 1988
# and to the public at the NEC on 14 October 1988. Saloon and hatchback; the
# estate never materialised. Top of the UK large-family sector in 1990 ahead of
# the Sierra, and Britain's second best-selling car in 1992; revised in 1992/93
# (new grille, lamps and bumper mouldings). Replaced by the Vectra in late 1995.
# http://cavalierandchevetteclub.com/cavalier%20mk3%20saloon%20and%20hatch.htm
#
# Dimensions: 4,432 x 1,706 x 1,400 mm, wheelbase 2,600 mm.
# https://www.auto-data.net/en/vauxhall-cavalier-mk-iii-generation-1468
#
# Colours: Star Silver (1991-97), Satin Red (1991 on), Diamond Black (1990 on)
# and Nautilus Blue Mica (1994 on) are documented Vauxhall colours of the Mk3's
# years. https://www.vauxhallcavalier.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=2192
#
# Colour shares and weight: the Mk3 was the sector leader in 1990 and second
# best-seller overall in 1992, so it is set at 320 against the Escort's 500
# anchor, split silver 105, red 85, black 75, blue 55. Provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 170 km/h: a game-balance figure for the 1.4-2.5 range.
# Comfort 110/345: a 1990s family saloon, between the Mk2 Cavalier's 100/330 and
# the Sierra's 120/360; the line gives 345.
#
# Dates describe road presence: launch October 1988 with a 13-14 year tail,
# staggered by colour.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cavalier-mk3.blend in the blends
# repository. References: citycars/references/vauxhall-cavalier-mk3/ (gitignored).
# Image credits: 1992 Cavalier 1.6 photographs, Wikimedia Commons (see reference
# file names for the photographer and licence).

obj=citycar
